as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 2, "excerpt_id": "EXC_a35917034f591072", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_8b8761c1c81a24ac", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I’m starting to eat far less and constantly poke at my fat, starve, compare myself to other girls and today, I’ve given into regurgitating and that has made me almost lose it. I did mention in a previous post that I have a huge phobia of vomiting, and I see that it’s combatting my body dysmorphia now. I’m at my nerves end. I do have times where I’m calm and collected. Reading a book."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_501147e567f04538", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_89bb140615a300d3", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "Yesterday afternoon, two black males attacked me from behind, took my phone, and shoved me to the ground. The police came and did all the investigation he could and I came to my hotel I'm currently staying at (I'm traveling right now-yes female solo travel can be dangerous lol), slightly scraped and shaken but no major injuries. The police weren't hopeful that they will get to find my phone with all of my not-backed up travel photos but at least I survived the day and I can get a new phone! Money doesn't concern me, I'm just really bugged that I won't have all of my photos from two-week travel. The thing is, I was scrolling through youtube to find phone reviews (so that I can get a new one and not regret it lol) and clicked on a video with a black male person showed up.", "candidate_role": "counterevidence", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as a boundary case or counterexample.", "display_order": 3, "excerpt_id": "EXC_501147e567f04538", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_89bb140615a300d3", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Yesterday afternoon, two black males attacked me from behind, took my phone, and shoved me to the ground. The police came and did all the investigation he could and I came to my hotel I'm currently staying at (I'm traveling right now-yes female solo travel can be dangerous lol), slightly scraped and shaken but no major injuries. The police weren't hopeful that they will get to find my phone with all of my not-backed up travel photos but at least I survived the day and I can get a new phone! Money doesn't concern me, I'm just really bugged that I won't have all of my photos from two-week travel. The thing is, I was scrolling through youtube to find phone reviews (so that I can get a new one and not regret it lol) and clicked on a video with a black male person showed up."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 4, "excerpt_id": "EXC_87225c2d98e4040e", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_7b6ac9fd06046be8", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I'm in a nursing program, and we're talking about domestic violence. It just so happens this lecture has been on the syllabus since day one, I just have impeccable timing. My question is, should I talk to my cohort about my experience? I feel that it may make them more aware to see and speak to someone that's been in the situation. I feel its important they know how police treated me, and the fact that the first people that showed empathy, the first people that asked \"are you okay?\""}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 5, "excerpt_id": "EXC_2e111aad7138d8f9", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_f9a9184a50b7e7ab", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Read from your sheet and you will be accepted by others effortlessly. This also starts the beginning of you allowing yourself to be yourself. Do you believe strongly about animal rights ? Brilliant that would go down pretty well in the court? Sounds commendable, put it on your sheet and read from it."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_4fb972e20f0edab9", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_cf92fbdbf3888e38", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "I've had other things happening - lack of direction in life, nervousness about getting a job, feeling lonely by neglecting friends to do work and internships. I don't know if I don't love him anymore. I don't know if I can get past my resentment. I don't know. **Tl'dr: I feel numb to my boyfriend after a series of arguments/events that have left me not feeling loved or like a priority to my boyfriend.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 6, "excerpt_id": "EXC_4fb972e20f0edab9", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_cf92fbdbf3888e38", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I've had other things happening - lack of direction in life, nervousness about getting a job, feeling lonely by neglecting friends to do work and internships. I don't know if I don't love him anymore. I don't know if I can get past my resentment. I don't know. **Tl'dr: I feel numb to my boyfriend after a series of arguments/events that have left me not feeling loved or like a priority to my boyfriend."}], "item_id": "DJI_548eaf058cb181bb", "item_schema_version": "direction-j-evaluator-item-v1", "output_id": "OUT_548eaf058cb181bb", "packet_id": "PKT_390996e7007912b9", "proposed_interpretation": {"boundary_conditions": ["The context is a private online forum where individuals share their personal experiences and emotions.", "The excerpts are from different source units, indicating diverse perspectives on stress."], "claim": "Individuals describe stress as an overwhelming emotional state that can be triggered by various life events or circumstances.", "explanation": "The excerpts suggest that individuals experience stress in response to specific situations, such as a physical attack (EXC_501147e567f04538), relationship issues (EXC_4fb972e20f0edab9), or body image concerns (EXC_a35917034f591072).", "theme_id": "THM_548eaf058cb181bb", "theme_name": "Stress and emotional states"}, "research_question": "How do people describe and contextualize experiences of stress?", "source_coverage": {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 3, "candidate_cited_source_count": 3, "coverage_note": "Counts describe only this restricted private packet.", "presented_excerpt_count": 6, "presented_source_count": 6, "sampling_frame_excerpt_count": 6, "sampling_frame_source_count": 6, "source_distribution": [{"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_401d4e50f0d19732"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_7b6ac9fd06046be8"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_89bb140615a300d3"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_8b8761c1c81a24ac"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_cf92fbdbf3888e38"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_f9a9184a50b7e7ab"}]}}

